- @next: Vice President George H W Bush has won the presidential election, securing a third consecutive Republican term in the White House.

@next

His Democratic party rival Michael Dukakis seemingly failed to capitalise on dissatisfaction with the outgoing administration with Bush having presented himself as the natural successor to Reagan's political legacy.

This means a continuation of the Reagan administration's general direction, particularly in foreign policy and economic affairs, though Bush may seek to establish a more pragmatic approach of his own. The Republican victory ensures that Washington's existing course will remain largely intact.
